& [ManualReviewCorrections] is implemented fault-driven hardening
  + [scope_content] is every unit kind and perspective constrained by the signed package authority scope
  + [scope_request] is query package scope constrained by the enclosing protocol request scope
  + [package_set] is the runtime package set unique and exactly equal to caller bindings
  + [semantic_completeness] is blank meaning, alias, source set, source path, relation source, proof identity, dependency identity or version, and compiler version rejected before signing
  + [Unicode_source] is every quoted byte span constrained to valid UTF-8 character boundaries
  + [strict_machine_form] is unknown nested state, package, query, result, and protocol fields rejected rather than ignored
  + [bounded_identity_fault] is invalid long semantic identity reported by byte length and bounded preview rather than echoed in full
  + [bounded_query_fault] is long unknown caller text reported by bounded preview and byte length rather than echoed in full
  + [bounded_explanation] is per-candidate scoring explanation count capped with visible omission accounting
  + [exact_index] is normalized exact and alias lookup served from the admission-verified signed index
  + [global_identity] is semantic-unit and relation identities unique across the loaded package set
  + [empty_term] is whitespace query input invalid rather than a lexical wildcard
  + [request_completeness] is blank selectors and missing requested-detail demand rejected before lookup
  + [authority_detail] is package proof accounted independently from record projection clipping
  + [resident_detail] is a caller-resident unit suppresses only redundant record transmission and not newly requested source proof
  + [inspection_proof] is inspect results digest-bound and semantic-unit inspection includes the signed source-document digest
  + [continuation] is a closed typed protocol value verified against status
  + [fault_projection] is partial protocol faults exactly equal core query faults
  + [strong_verification] is exact deterministic re-execution available against a supervisor-pinned signed environment

