& [ExplicitNonclaimSet] is retained honesty
  + [security_review] is a focused implementation audit and test expansion rather than a third-party penetration test or formal verification
  + [dependency_scan] is only as current and complete as the recorded RustSec database
  + [response_digest] is consistency rather than authentication when an attacker can replace content and digest together
  + [response_authenticity] remains the supervisor's trusted-executable and local-channel responsibility
  + [keys] are public fixture keys and never production authority
  + [signer_operation] is distinct cryptographic keys and roles but not production separation of duty because the fixture compiler process holds both signers
  + [time_replay] is environment time operator-supplied and coordinated replay of an old request plus once-valid environment requires supervisor anti-rollback policy
  + [caller_authentication] is absent; Cantor enforces declared scope containment while the supervisor must authenticate caller identity and derive ACL scope
  + [relation_boundary] is relationship edges package-local until a separately governed cross-package link authority exists
  + [canonical_interchange] is deterministic version-locked Rust serde_json rather than a proven cross-language canonical encoding
  + [persistence] is in-memory only
  + [MCP] is inactive_at_this_audit_capture; CEB-014 and CEB-015 were subsequently activated and passed under the linked separate proof
  + [neural_routing] is inactive
  + [FPGA] is inactive
  + [provider_inference] is inactive
  + [service_and_effects] are inactive
  + [git_disposition] is audited changes remain unstaged in the preexisting broad working tree pending an intentional commit boundary

